# Code Style Guide — DNA Music

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` in all tsconfig files.
- Prefer `interface` for public contracts; `type` for unions and mapped types.
- Named exports in domain modules; default exports only for page-level React components.
- `readonly` on immutable DTO properties.

## Naming conventions

| Scope | Convention | Example |
| ----- | ---------- | ------- |
| Backend files | kebab-case | `student.service.ts` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `StudentService` |
| Functions / variables | camelCase | `findById` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_FILE_SIZE` |
| Prisma enums | PascalCase name, SCREAMING_SNAKE values | `StudentStatus.ACTIVO` |
| React components | PascalCase file + export | `StudentsPage.tsx` |
| Hook files | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useStudentQueries.ts` |
| Repository files | `{entity}.repository.ts` | `user.repository.ts` |
| Type files | `{entity}.types.ts` | `student.types.ts` |

## Backend (`api/`)

- One module = one folder under `src/`.
- Controllers: HTTP only → services.
- Services: business logic + Prisma.
- DTOs: `class-validator` input DTOs + `*-response.dto.ts` for output.
- Error constants: `*-errors.constants.ts` per module.
- Public Prisma selects: `*-public.select.ts` to avoid leaking fields.

## Frontend (`web/`)

```text
pages/        → thin composition
hooks/        → data orchestration (queries + mutations per domain)
repositories/ → service adapters behind interfaces
services/     → Axios HTTP only
mappers/      → form → payload
types/        → domain types (split by entity)
components/   → UI, dialogs, CRUD table
context/      → React context (toast)
store/        → Redux auth only
utils/        → validation, formatting, confirm helpers
```

- HTTP calls only in `services/`.
- Hooks call `repositories/`, never `services/` directly from pages.
- Form dialogs in `components/{entity}/`; shared table in `components/crud/`.

## Formatting

- Prettier: single quotes, ES5 trailing commas, `printWidth: 120`.
- ESLint: zero warnings in CI; `no-explicit-any` is error.

## Commit messages

- `feat(scope): description`
- `fix(scope): description`
- `refactor(scope): description`
- `docs: description`
- `chore: description`
- `test: description`
